 61CR c  2009Cr02: {+61}Cr produced in {+9}Be({+76}Ge,X) reaction at a beam     
 61CR2c  energy of 130 MeV/nucleon. The {+76}Ge beam was produced by the        
 61CR3c  coupled cyclotrons at the National Superconducting Cyclotron           
 61CR4c  Laboratory at Michigan State University. Fragments were separated      
 61CR5c  using the A1900 fragment separator. The |b and |g spectra were measured
 61CR6c  using the Beta Counting System and the Segmented Germanium Array, as   
 61CR7c  well as three Si PIN detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g, |b, |b|g coin,
 61CR8c  (fragment)|b coin, half-life of the {+61}Cr ground state.              
